{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 complete — RED→GREEN fix implemented, committed (Change-Id I5ecbef2, local HEAD c2505ef96cb2), pushing to Gerrit\n\n**Problem (confirmed).** The read-only MCP tools `render_workflow` and `get_workflow_status` returned `error:\"llm_unavailable\"` for caller-input / not-found cases. Root cause (per Phase-1 RCA): the WorkflowError subtree subclasses LLMError, and `error_code_for` (_errors.py) blanket-mapped every LLMError → llm_unavailable. A second hard-coded site existed at `_structured_llm_failure` (_mcp_llm.py).\n\n**Proof (held-out oracle).** Added tests/interfaces/contracts/test_workflow_error_codes_dbca.py (7 tests) driving the ACTUAL MCP read tools and `error_code_for`. Confirmed RED for the right reasons before the fix; GREEN after. A sandboxed mutation check (seed the defect back) returned the 4 behaviour tests to RED and left the 3 base-guard tests green; restoring the fix returned all green.\n\n**Fix (per-subclass, NOT a blanket flip).**\n- Added `not_found` + `invalid_input` to the exported `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (schemas/common.schema.json + docs/mcp-reference.md + regenerated tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json).\n- New `WorkflowNotFoundError(WorkflowError)` raised at the 4 not-found sites in runs.py (unknown workflow name; unknown run_id; run absent from ticket ×2) → `not_found`. Optional `source=` kwarg preserves the `<name>: workflow '<name>' not found ...` message shape.\n- WorkflowParseError / WorkflowValidationError / WorkflowVersionError (found but won't parse/lint/migrate) → `invalid_input`.\n- The bare `WorkflowError` base (the EXECUTE base) DELIBERATELY still maps to `llm_unavailable` — an execute step can genuinely fail on LLM outage. **AC3 protected.**\n- Classifier logic centralised in `error_code_for` via extracted `_workflow_caller_code` helper (keeps McCabe ≤15, no baseline bump). `_structured_llm_failure` now delegates to `error_code_for` so both LLM-tier sites share one taxonomy.\n\n**Defect origin (caused_by, confirmed).** Same class as the Phase-1 finding: the blanket LLMError→llm_unavailable mapping introduced in 8a31-e1c3-cf31-4239 (biomedical-upper-tench, commit 77f1c4011c83). Close class: plan_defect (same as closed fixes wolflike-chevroned-haddock, dear-name-ladle).\n\n**Scope & safety.** Caller-dependency sweep: the only `except WorkflowParseError` catchers (schema.py, lint.py) are on the parse-text path, which the name-resolution not-found does not traverse; CLI catches broad WorkflowError; `pytest.raises(WorkflowError, match=...)` in test_workflow_entrypoints.py still holds because WorkflowNotFoundError IS-A WorkflowError. Regression: full sweep tests/unit/workflow/ + tests/interfaces/contracts/ + test_workflow_entrypoints + llm failure matrix = 1172 passed; targeted envelope/render/api-surface = 46 passed. make lint (incl. complexity baseline new=0 increased=0) + make typecheck (683 files) clean.\n\n**Siblings (escalated, NOT fixed — needed a new design decision).** Two more bare-WorkflowError sites still collapse to llm_unavailable: executor.py:541 (unknown scripted step) and editor.py:475 (missing editor bundle). Filed as fightable-nirvanic-kitten (35ab-f0e0-3e4a-4b72), linked discovered_from this ticket. Left out of scope per operator direction to escalate new error-code design decisions.\n\n**Residual risk.** Low. Vocabulary additions are additive/backward-compatible; the reclassification is confined to the WorkflowError subtree via a dedicated not-found subclass, with execute-time outages provably preserved.\n\n**Replication.** Original report no longer reproduces end-to-end: both `render_workflow` (unknown name) and `get_workflow_status` (unknown run_id) now return `not_found` through the real MCP tools.\n\nNext: push to Gerrit; await LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1; Submit; then close with --class=plan_defect --caused-by=8a31-e1c3-cf31-4239."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787957804093962001,"uuid":"47d537b5-6286-4ee1-a2c8-a78082746cd2"}